      "title": "Tunisians",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tunisians",
      "intro": "Tunisians are the citizens and nationals of Tunisia in North Africa, who speak Tunisian Arabic and/or one of the Berber languages commonly found in Southern Tunisia and share a common Tunisian culture and identity. In addition to the approximately 12 million residents in Tunisia, a Tunisian diaspora has been established with modern migration, particularly in Western Europe, namely France, Italy and Germany. The vast majority of Tunisians are Arabs and Berbers who adhere to Sunni Islam."
